rem Find the 200th Prime-proof sqube
rem containing the contiguous sub-string
rem "200"
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=200
rem Find the Nth number p^2 q^3, p and q
rem distinct primes, that contains 200
rem and stays composite when any one of
rem its digits is changed

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 200
arg Bound integer = 300000000000

rem List the squbes up to Bound, keep
rem those with 200 inside, and test each
rem change of one digit for primality.
Top = (Bound / 4) ** (1 / 3) floor + 1
All = array shape 0 fill 0
for Q in primes to Top
  Cube = Q * Q * Q
  Lim = (Bound // Cube) isqrt
  Ps = primes to Lim array
  Ps = Ps filter (Ps not equal Q) array
  All = concat All (Ps * Ps * Cube)
end
Sorted = All sort
Pos = (0 to 12 array) reshape 1 13
Pw = 10 ** Pos
Rows = Sorted len
Col' = Sorted reshape Rows 1
Win' = Col // Pw mod 1000
Has' = (Win equal 200) any axis 1
Cand = Sorted filter Has array
Cnt = Cand len
X3 = Cand reshape Cnt 1 1
Cur = (X3 // (Pw reshape 1 13 1)) mod 10
Ds = (0 to 9 array) reshape 1 1 10
P3 = Pw reshape 1 13 1
Y' = X3 - Cur * P3 + Ds * P3
Real' = P3 at most X3 and Ds not equal Cur
Cells = Cnt * 130
Prime' = (Y reshape Cells) in primes
Flat' = Prime reshape Cnt 130
Ok' = Real reshape Cnt 130
Bad' = Flat and Ok
Proof' = not (Bad any axis 1)
Good' = Cand filter Proof array
Answer = Good (N - 1)
Answer print
